<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* Fallback only — every routable page sets its own <PageTitle>. Kept in the same
       "PoPunkouterSoftware — <section>" form as those so the brand never varies. *@
    <title>PoPunkouterSoftware</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="images/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon" />
    @* No Google Fonts link here, deliberately. Radzen.Blazor already ships the Material
       Symbols variable font and self-hosts it under the family name "Material Symbols";
       every <RadzenIcon> in the app has always used that copy. The remote stylesheet was
       serving only the four bare <span class="material-symbols-outlined"> glyphs in
       MainLayout, and charging first paint for them: a render-blocking cross-origin
       stylesheet, two preconnects, and — because the URL carried no `display=swap` — a
       font whose default `display:auto` left those header icons blank until a third-party
       round trip completed. modern-ui.css now declares the same family against the local
       file, so the header icons and the Radzen ones resolve from one same-origin request
       that was already being made. Re-adding this link would reintroduce the block. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/boot.css" />
    @* Radzen ships one stylesheet per theme and its component colours are baked in — they
       do not follow prefers-color-scheme. Loading only software-dark.css meant that in
       light mode every Radzen surface (data grid, paginator, badges, base text) kept
       dark-theme values while the page around them flipped. Each sheet is now scoped to
       the scheme it was built for. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Radzen.Blazor/css/software.css" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Radzen.Blazor/css/software-dark.css" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/modern-ui.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="PoPunkouterSoftware.Client.styles.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
@* No `rz-background-color-base rz-color-base` here: both resolve to `var(--rz-base)`
   (#505f65) with `!important`, so every heading that did not set its own colour
   inherited a mid-slate grey — washed out in light mode and dim in dark. The page's
   background and text come from --app-bg-deep / --app-text in modern-ui.css. *@
<body>
    @* Single GPU compositing layer for the whole app — see js/gpu-backdrop.js.
       Stays invisible (and the CSS grid fallback stays visible) unless WebGL
       initialises successfully. *@
    <canvas id="app-gpu-backdrop" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div id="app-nav-progress"></div>
    <div id="app-boot-splash" aria-label="Loading">
        <div class="app-boot-spinner"></div>
        <div class="app-boot-label">Loading PoPunkouterSoftware…</div>
    </div>
    <Routes />
    <script>
        // Suppress expected hotreload errors in development
        const originalError = console.error;
        console.error = function(...args) {
            const msg = args[0]?.toString?.() || '';
            if (msg.includes('blazor-hotreload') || msg.includes('net::ERR_ABORTED')) {
                return;  // Silently ignore hotreload connection errors
            }
            originalError.apply(console, args);
        };
        // Remove the boot splash the moment Blazor renders real UI (the Radzen layout).
        (function () {
            // Re-query on every call: an enhanced navigation re-inserts a *brand new*
            // splash element (the server renders one into every response, and the DOM
            // diff restores what we removed), so a captured reference goes stale.
            // `fade` is for the cold load only — on navigation the splash must vanish
            // instantly or every page change flashes a full-screen overlay for 300ms.
            window.dismissBootSplash = function (fade) {
                var splash = document.getElementById('app-boot-splash');
                if (!splash) return;
                if (!fade) { splash.remove(); return; }
                splash.classList.add('is-dismissed');
                setTimeout(function () { splash.remove(); }, 350);
            };

            var observer = new MutationObserver(function () {
                if (document.querySelector('.rz-layout, .app-topbar')) {
                    observer.disconnect();
                    window.dismissBootSplash(true);
                }
            });
            observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
            // Fail-safe: never trap the user behind the splash if boot detection misses.
            setTimeout(function () { observer.disconnect(); window.dismissBootSplash(true); }, 30000);
        })();
        // Navigation progress bar for Blazor enhanced navigation.
        (function () {
            var bar = null;
            function getBar() { return bar || (bar = document.getElementById('app-nav-progress')); }
            window.appNavStart = function () {
                var b = getBar(); if (!b) return;
                b.className = 'is-active';
                // Close the mobile drawer once a navigation begins, otherwise it stays
                // open across page changes and looks like a stuck overlay.
                if (window.closeTopbarDrawer) window.closeTopbarDrawer();
            };
            window.appNavEnd = function () {
                var b = getBar(); if (!b) return;
                b.className = 'is-done';
                setTimeout(function () {
                    b.className = 'is-hidden';
                    setTimeout(function () { b.className = ''; }, 300);
                }, 200);
            };
        })();
    </script>
    @* Load order is load-bearing. motion-kit.js defines window.motionKit, the single rAF
       governor every animated layer subscribes to, so it must come first. audio-kit.js is
       next because gpu-backdrop.js and starfield-backdrop.js both PULL window.audioKit.energy()
       inside their frame callbacks (they null-check it, so the order is defensive rather
       than strictly required — but a first frame without audio coupling is a visible pop). *@
    <script src="js/motion-kit.js"></script>
    <script src="js/audio-kit.js"></script>
    <script src="js/helpers.js"></script>
    @* The WebGL2/WebGL1 renderer. Always loaded: it is the tier nearly every visitor
       actually gets, and the fallback for the one above it. The WebGPU renderer is NOT
       declared here — gpu-backdrop.js fetches js/gfx-webgpu.js itself, and only when
       navigator.gpu exists, so a browser that cannot use a line of it never downloads it. *@
    <script src="js/gfx-webgl.js"></script>
    <script src="js/gpu-backdrop.js"></script>
    @* Small wrapper only (no THREE dependency at parse time) — it lazily fetches
       lib/three/three.min.js itself, and only when starfieldBackdrop.init() is called
       from Index.razor. Loading it here costs every route a few KB; the actual ~600KB
       Three.js payload only ever downloads for a visit to "/". See the file header in
       js/starfield-backdrop.js for the full cost-scoping rationale. *@
    <script src="js/starfield-backdrop.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
    @* Enhanced-navigation callbacks are delivered through Blazor's own listener registry,
       NOT as DOM events — `document.addEventListener('enhancedload', ...)` never fires and
       silently does nothing. Must come after blazor.web.js, which is what defines `Blazor`.

       Without the splash hookup, clicking an in-app link leaves the re-inserted boot splash
       covering a fully rendered page forever (the first-load MutationObserver is already
       disconnected by then), which looks exactly like the app hanging on load. *@
    <script>
        Blazor.addEventListener('enhancednavigationstart', window.appNavStart);
        Blazor.addEventListener('enhancedload', function () {
            window.dismissBootSplash(false);
            window.appNavEnd();
        });
    </script>
    <script src="_content/Radzen.Blazor/Radzen.Blazor.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

